# Native macOS Host installer

Branch: `macos-installer`, starting at main e7121a2.

Goal: open one signed, notarized PKG in Installer, approve administrator access,
and install the Host without Terminal, Python, Xcode or Command Line Tools on
the destination Mac. macOS 27/Apple Silicon only. macOS privacy consent remains
explicit and cannot be granted by this installer.

1. Verify Developer ID Application and Developer ID Installer private-key
   identities on the dedicated development Mac. Never use the Mac App Store
   installer identity for this package. Keep notarization credentials in Keychain.
2. Implement a narrow native installation helper, executed only by Installer's
   root pre/post-install scripts. Retain configuration, private identities,
   protected log creation, bounded graphical-worker/coordinator drain, and
   system-wide LoginWindow/Aqua startup. Use system tools by absolute paths;
   no downloadable runtime or Python dependency on the target.
3. Use ordinary payload/receipt-based PKG installation to /Applications. Reject
   alternate volumes, unsupported OS/architecture, unsafe filesystem objects,
   unrelated existing apps/jobs and signer mismatch before stopping services.
   Retain the previous app for recovery. The deliberate Apple Development to
   same-team Developer ID transition needs explicit permission continuity tests;
   do not silently claim existing TCC grants survive it.
4. Sign the app with hardened runtime and a secure timestamp, sign the installer
   with Developer ID Installer, notarize and staple the final PKG. Keep the
   production download unavailable until signature/notarization gates pass.
5. Test helper failure paths without changing services, inspect package payload,
   scripts, version and signatures, then obtain authorization to exercise real
   install/upgrade on development-mac. Never interrupt its session or reboot automatically.
   Test fresh-machine absence of Python/developer tools and permission workflow.
6. Provide a graphical uninstall path with the same bounded shutdown and
   preserved settings/certificates/logs. Do not present the existing Python
   development uninstaller as the production operator workflow.

Current checkpoint: both Developer ID identities are valid and use the existing
Team ID. The operator created Keychain profile `plank-notary`; authenticated
notarization history query succeeds. Native helper, payload scripts, graphical
installer/uninstaller descriptions and signed/notarized build runner implemented
for 1.0.80-macos-installer. Initial 44 policy checks and 62 checks with the root
filesystem fixture pass; bounded-drain simulations are being added. Existing
development installer still passes all 17 tests. Read-only preflight passes
against development-mac, including the same-team development signature. No installed Host,
permissions, services or streaming code changed. Live install/upgrade/uninstall,
fresh-machine and permission continuity gates remain open.
